{
  "requirement": "Every defined example MUST have an `evidence/<full-example-name>.json` file whose `example` string exactly matches the current example body. A true determination MUST have at least one `{test}` reference to the example, covered by an evidence input. The reviewer MUST assess its tests under {cite}`requirements.ci.review_criteria` and use the outcomes defined by {cite}`requirements.ci.outcomes`; the no-test justification for a requirement MUST NOT establish a true example judgment. Habeas MUST apply the same missing-evidence, determination, input validation, and reference-coverage checks used for requirements. It MUST report a true determination with no test reference and changed example text with a compact line-oriented diff.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: true.** The marked code implements each obligation of `requirements.examples.evidence`, and the tests cover the main success and failure cases. One small marking risk (see Gaps) does not change the verdict.\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Evidence file exists for every example.** `inspect_repository_with_progress` in `src/evidence.rs` reports `evidence/<name>.json: missing for example …` for every non-term definition with no evidence file. Examples are included, and the file name is the full example name. `DefinitionKind::noun` in `src/lib.rs` supplies the \"example\" wording and the `example` field name.\n- **`example` string matches the current body.** `validate_evidence_file` selects the field name from the definition kind (`example` or `requirement`) and compares the recorded text with the declaration text. A mismatch reports `example text changed (<source>)` followed by `compact_diff` output, which is the compact line-oriented diff the requirement asks for. It also reports a missing `example` field and an unexpected `requirement` field.\n- **True determination needs a `{test}` reference covered by an input.** `validate_references` in `src/evidence.rs` reports `example X has a true determination but no {test} reference` when the example has no `{test}` reference or `:test:` anchor and the evidence determination is `true`. `FIXME` and `false` do not trigger this check. For each non-`{cite}` reference it also requires an evidence input that covers the reference line, and reports `no input covers {test}…` otherwise. Anchors get an equivalent check.\n- **Same checks as for requirements.** Examples go through the same code path as requirements: missing evidence, determination parsing (a false determination is an error), input hash and text validation, the reference-set digest, and reference coverage.\n- **Reviewer behaviour.** `initial_prompt` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` builds the prompt from the definition template. The test `initial_prompt_carries_the_review_criteria` shows the prompt contains the example-specific criterion (\"For an example, assess whether test setup and assertions cover its scenario and expected outcomes … Explain the coverage.\"). The outcome guidance (`true`, `FIXME`, `false`) is also tested. Whether the prompt also bars a requirement's no-test justification from establishing a true example judgment was not verified.\n\n**Tests**\n- `cited_example_with_a_test_and_matching_evidence_validates` (`src/evidence.rs`) covers:\n  - a valid example with a test and covering inputs;\n  - an uncovered test reference (`no input covers` at `src/main.rs:1`);\n  - a changed test input hash;\n  - a changed requirements glob;\n  - changed example text, with the `- Outdated.` diff;\n  - a wrong field name (`missing field \"example\"`, `unexpected field \"requirement\"`);\n  - a deleted evidence file (`missing for example`).\n- `example_errors_include_duplicates_invalid_bodies_and_missing_tests` covers a true determination with no `{test}` reference.\n- `tests/outcomes.rs::fixme_examples_pass_without_test_references_but_true_examples_do_not` shows a `FIXME` example passes without a test reference, a `true` example fails with \"no {test} reference\", and a `false` example is rejected.\n\n**Gaps**\n- `compact_diff` is marked only `ci.diagnostics`, not `examples.evidence`. It is a generic diff helper called from the marked function, so I did not treat this as a gap.",
